 to the horizon `H`.\\n- Optional features, each a **proposal**: instance normalization over (L,H) on inputs and inverse-renormalized targets (RevIN-style affine), multi-scale stacking by repeating the cycle decomposition for several candidate `w` values and summing predictions.\\n- I will **not** propose multi-scale stacking or RevIN by default; flagged below as must-confirm.\\n\\n**(b) Datasets** *(proposal — unconfirmed; nothing in `/workspace` specifies them)*\\n- Candidate set, all commonly used in time-series-forecasting practice: Exchange, Weather, ETTh1/ETTh2/ETTm1/ETTm2, Electricity, Traffic, ILI. **Assumed** characteristics:\\n  - ETTh*: hourly, daily/weekly periodicity (`w=24`).\\n  - ETTm*: 15-min, daily/weekly (`w=96`).\\n  - Electricity / Traffic: hourly, daily/weekly (`w=24`).\\n  - Exchange: daily business-day series, weak periodicity (`w=5`).\\n  - Weather: 10-min, daily (`w=144`).\\n  - ILI: weekly, yearly (`w=52`).\\n- These numbers are **assumptions from general knowledge of common benchmarks**; the task description does not name a dataset and nothing in `/workspace` confirms any of them.\\n\\n**(c) Task formulation**\\n- Horizons `H`: for ETT classics `{96, 192, 336, 720}` (proposal); ILI `{24, 36, 48, 60}`; Exchange `{96, 192, 336, 720}`; Weather/Electricity/Traffic — **must confirm**.\\n- Lookback `L`: tuned over a small candidate set, e.g. `{L ∈ {96, 192, 336, 720}}` with constraint `L % w == 0`; carrying over the convention that `L = 2*w` or matching each dataset's common setting. **Proposal — must confirm.**\\n- Univariate vs multivariate: report both for multivariate datasets (predict all channels jointly); univariate reported **only** for `OT` column in ETTh*/ETTm* per common convention. **Proposal — must confirm.**\\n- Normalization: train-set-mean/std (or median/IQR) computed on the **training split only**, applied per channel. If RevIN-like affine is added, recompute stats per window inside the model and invert at the output. **Proposal — must confirm.**\\n- Splits: standard fixed splits used in time-series forecasting benchmarks (e.g., ETT 7:1:2 for {h1,h2}, 6:2:2 for {m1,m2}; commonly cited 70/10/20 or 60/20/20 for Electricity/Traffic; rolling test on the last `H × N_windows` steps). **Proposal — must confirm.**\\n- First `L` samples: predictor starts producing forecasts only once a full lookback is available; no padding on the input — earlier windows are simply not generated.\\n\\n**(d) Training setup** *(proposals — must confirm)*\\n- Optimizer: Adam with `weight_decay ∈ {1e-4, 1e-5}`, `amsgrad=False` (default).\\n- LR: cosine from peak `lr ∈ {1e-3, 5e-4, 1e-4}` to ~1% of peak (one-cycle and fixed-LR alternatives mentioned but **not selected**).\\n- Batch size: `{32, 64}`.\\n- Epochs: `{50, 100, 200}` with **early stopping on validation loss** (patience ~10).\\n- Loss: MSE on **standardized targets** for backprop; report both **MSE and MAE** on the original scale at evaluation time.\\n- Gradient clipping: max-norm `1.0`.\\n- Seed averaging: report mean ± std over `N_seeds = 3` on every metric, every horizon.\\n\\n**(e) Evaluation**\\n- Primary metrics: MSE and MAE on each horizon.\\n- MSE computed on **standardized targets**; MAE on the original scale for interpretability. **Proposal — must confirm.**\\n- Protocol: **multi-horizon over all rolling windows** that fit fully inside the test split with stride `= H` (no overlap); alternative is a single fixed-anchor test window repeated over seeds. **Proposal — must confirm.**\\n- Report per-horizon and an unweighted mean over horizons.\\n\\n**(f) Baselines**\\n- Must-include: (i) **naïve last-value** (`ŷ[t+1:t+H] = x[t]`); (ii) **seasonal-naïve at `w`** (`ŷ[t+h] = x[t+h−w]`, shifted into the forecast window); (iii) **DLinear-style linear model** (two parallel linear layers on trend/seasonal split) — directly comparable to CycleNet.\\n- Discussion-only (do **not** promise to implement if compute is tight): a vanilla Transformer or FEDformer-style 