Transformer-family reference even if compute is tight.\\n10. **Language of delivered write-up** — Hindi or English.\\n\\n**Nice-to-have**\\n- FFT/autocorrelation period auto-detection as an arm or as the default.\\n- Multi-scale CycleNet stacking ablation by default or only if time permits.\\n- Additional metrics beyond MSE/MAE (MAPE, CRPS).\\n- Exact seed count (3 vs 5) for variance reporting.\\n- L1 vs L2 as the optimization objective when ablations are toggled.\\n\\n---\\n\\nAwaiting your direction on the **must-confirm** items before producing the full design (rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility write-up) in a subsequent `stage=result` turn.\",\"evidence\":\"Workspace contents under /workspace: only task.json is present; `python3 --version` reports 3.12.3 and a naive `import numpy` fails with ModuleNotFoundError, confirming the no-preinstalled-dependencies constraint. The 'track.md' cited in your message is the documents.track.md field inside task.json, whose full body is one line: 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.' No prior code, datasets, or results exist in /workspace; all architecture and benchmark specifics above are proposals drawn from general knowledge of CycleNet-style models, not from in-repo artifacts.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Qualitative (not quantified) CPU 24-thread feasibility: cycle indices and a small linear head dominate throughput, but no fabricated per-epoch runtimes are claimed.</item>\",\"$text\":\"Proposal (must confirm): Naive last-value, seasonal-naive at w, and DLinear are the must-include baselines; a Transformer-family reference is a nice-to-have discussion item.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Proposal (must confirm): RevIN-like window-wise affine normalization is offered as an opt-in on top of plain per-channel train-set statistics.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Proposals (must confirm): horizon sets H={96,192,336,720} for ETT/Exchange-style, plus ILI {24,36,48,60},