{"id": "c606a34c-f5a6-4460-858a-fcce4def9db2", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T19:42:59.504342", "source": "user", "parent_id": "c9c6e5df-3032-4971-bd95-04d674c9afd9", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach approved with the following explicit resolutions to all must-confirm items so you can produce the full design without further back-and-forth. Treat each locked choice below as the design default; deviations must be flagged in-text as assumptions. (1) Periodicity: design defaults to dataset-known canonical periods (ETTh* w=24 hourly-daily; ETTm* w=96 15-min-daily; Electricity/Traffic w=24 hourly-daily; Exchange w=5 business-day; Weather w=144 10-min-daily; ILI w=52 weekly-yearly). Auto-detect-w via FFT/autocorrelation is an OPTIONAL ABLATION ARM only, NOT the default. (2) Datasets: use the standard CycleNet benchmark set — ETTh1, ETTh2, ETTm1, ETTm2, Weather, Exchange, Electricity, Traffic, ILI. Note that Electricity/Traffic/Weather/Exchange downloads are not feasible in the bubblewrap sandbox with disabled network; the design must state that data access is out of scope for design-only and that all per-dataset numbers are specification, not measured. (3) Horizons H: ETT/Exchange/Weather/Electricity/Traffic → {96, 192, 336, 720}; ILI → {24, 36, 48, 60}. (4) Lookback L: tuned over {96, 192, 336, 720} with constraint L % w == 0, selecting best on validation MSE; report L used per dataset. (5) Reporting convention: multivariate (all channels) is the primary reported result; univariate on the OT column for ETT families is reported as a secondary result, clearly labeled. (6) Normalization: default = plain per-channel train-set mean/std computed only on the training split. RevIN-like per-window affine normalization is reported as a separate ablation arm (off by default in the main run). (7) Loss for backprop: MSE on standardized targets; evaluation reports both MSE and MAE on the original scale. L1 ablation is included as a sensitivity check. (8) Optimizer/schedule/regularization: Adam (amsgrad=False), weight_decay ∈ {1e-4, 1e-5}, gradient clip max-norm 1.0, cosine LR from peak ∈ {1e-3, 5e-4, 1e-4} to ~1% of peak; batch size ∈ {32, 64}; epochs up to {100, 200}, early stopping on validation MSE with patience 10. (9) Seeds: N_seeds = 3; report mean ± std for every (dataset, horizon, metric). (10) Evaluation protocol: multi-horizon rolling evaluation over all test windows with stride = H, no window overlap; report per-horizon and unweighted mean. (11) Baselines: must-include = last-value naive, seasonal-naive at w, DLinear. Transformer-family reference (a vanilla Transformer forecaster) is a NICE-TO-HAVE discussion item only — include a clear write-up of what would be compared against it, but if compute is tight the design should state it is omitted and recommend it as future work rather than fabricating numbers. (12) Ablations (priority-ordered): (a) fixed w vs auto-detected w via FFT/autocorrelation; (b) residual decomposition depth K (single-residual vs multi-cycle residual); (c) multi-scale CycleNet stacking on/off (NICE-TO-HAVE — may be relegated to a 'future-work' paragraph if it bloats the matrix); (d) normalization: per-channel train-stats vs RevIN-like window-wise affine; (e) loss MSE vs MAE; (f) per-channel independent head vs shared head. The ablation matrix must be sized so total CPU wall-clock is bounded — give an order-of-magnitude feasibility estimate (low-tens to low-hundreds of CPU-hours) and explicitly shrink N_seeds or drop the multi-scale arm if it overflows. (13) Controls: same splits, same normalization stats, same L, same H, same pipeline across every compared model; leakage checks (time-disjoint splits, no future in normalization, no rolling leaks) explicitly enumerated; variance reported across seeds. (14) Feasibility section: must be qualitative / order-of-magnitude only, no fabricated per-epoch times. State that runtime is bubblewrap with disabled network, no preinstalled Python deps (Python 3.12.3 verified; even numpy missing), 24 CPU threads only, no GPU. Dependency set reduced to numpy + torch (CPU build) + pandas + local CSVs/HDF5; document a pip-install step as a future execution prerequisite, NOT a current execution. (15) Language of the deliverable: write the design in Hindi per persona default, but keep all code, identifiers, dataset names, metric names, math notation, and the ablations table in their canonical English form so the document remains unambiguous. (16) Submission contract: final answer = a single experiment design document containing — in this order — (a) research question restatement, (b) CycleNet component specification (residual cycle-forecasting block, period w, decomposition, optional RevIN, optional multi-scale), (c) datasets and period assumptions table, (d) task formulation (H, L, splits, normalization, channels), (e) training/optimization recipe, (f) evaluation protocol and metrics, (g) baselines, (h) full ablation matrix with priority, (i) controls including leakage checks and seed protocol, (j) analysis plan including pre-registered comparison rules and what constitutes a 'better than DLinear' claim, (k) feasibility / risks given CPU-only bubblewrap no-network runtime, (l) explicit 'not run' statement. No executed experiments, no fabricated numbers, no GPU claims. Proceed now.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"result\", \"approach_approved\": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
