{"id": "481c8982-4b90-4aca-9c20-c7f99553b14f", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T19:46:42.406264", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "6c131260-c921-4b6d-9193-b64cb349eba9", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-3bd022ce-49e6-4a3a-a8fb-01887e95a4e7", "tool_call": {"id": "call-3bd022ce-49e6-4a3a-a8fb-01887e95a4e7", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Submit full CycleNet experiment design (Hindi narrative, English technical)\",\"stage\":\"result\",\"answer\":\"# CycleNet-style periodic time-series forecasting — experiment design\\n\\n> डिज़ाइन-मात्र दस्तावेज़। Execution नहीं हुआ है। सभी संख्याएँ specification हैं, मापी गई मान नहीं।\\n> Runtime: bubblewrap, network disabled, Python 3.12.3, no preinstalled numerical libraries (numpy भी नहीं), 24 CPU threads, no GPU.\\n> Workspace `/workspace` में केवल `task.json` है (≈395 bytes); `track.md` फ़ाइल磁盘 पर नहीं है — `task.json` का `documents.track.md` फ़ील्ड एक-पंक्ति वाला design-only नोट है।\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (a) Research question (पुनः-कथन)\\n\\nहम यह जाँचना चाहते हैं कि **CycleNet-शैली की residual-cycle forecasting architecture** का उपयोग करके **periodic structure वाले multivariate time-series** पर, **पूर्व-निर्धारित अवधि `w` के साथ (canonical / dataset-known)** और सामान्य benchmark datasets पर setting, **DLinear जैसे linear baselines से क्या तुलना में MSE / MAE मान आते हैं और कौन-से अवयव (residual decomposition depth, fixed vs auto-detected `w`, RevIN-style normalization, multi-scale stacking, loss choice) प्रभाव डालते हैं।**\\n\\nQuestion को operationally testable बनाने के लिए नीचे pre-registered comparison rule (अनुभाग (j)) दिया गया है — \\\"better than DLinear\\\" का दावा तभी होगा जब (i) average across `N_seeds=3` पर अंतर >0 और (ii) sign across seeds consistent हो।\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (b) CycleNet component specification\\n\\n### मूल ढाँचा (canonical high-level, well-supported at high level only)\\n\\nदिया हुआ lookback `X ∈ ℝ^{L × C}` जहाँ `L = lookback`, `C = number of channels`, और एक चुनी हुई canonical अवधि `w` (नीचे (c) की table के अनुसार)।\\n\\nमूल घटक (Block diagram — specification, not measured):\\n\\n```\\nX ∈ ℝ^{L × C}\\n   │\\n   ├──[Residual extraction]──── r_0 ∈ ℝ^{w × C}        (averaged over floor(L/w) whole cycles; take last w)\\n   │\\n   ├──[Cycle-indexed projection, K terms]───\\n   │      for k in {0, 1, …, K−1}:   r_k ∈ ℝ^{w × C}    (samples whose (t mod w) == k)\\n   │      sum(CycleIndexDecomp) restores L samples per channel\\n   │\\n   ├──[Residual cycle-forecasting block, per k]\\n   │      linear / small MLP on r_k[-w:] → o_k ∈ ℝ^{H × C}    (यानी आखिरी w samples पर apply)\\n   │\\n   ├──[Invert cycle-indexed projection]───\\n   │      for k in {0,1,…,H−1}: assign each target step h to offset index (h mod w), gathering o_{k}[h]\\n   │\\n   ├──[Linear / projection head]──→ Ŷ ∈ ℝ^{H × C}\\n```\\n\\n### घटक-दर-घटक विनिर्देश\\n\\n| घटक | Specification | Default | Optional arm | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Residual extraction (single) | epoch-wise averaging of full-cycle subsequences; **last `w`** rows retained | ON | — | **Baseline depth**; canonical \\\"1-cycle residual\\\" |\\n| Multi-cycle residual decomposition | ऊपर जैसा, पर `K = w` पूर्ण cycle indices | OFF (main run) | **Arm (b)** in (h) | Specification says K dim पर ablate |\\n| Cycle-indexed projection | `(t mod w)` द्वारा index, चैनल-वार | ON | — | Implementation note: efficient reshape `[B, L//w, w, C]` indexed operation |\\n| Forecasting block (residual cycle-forecasting) | per-(index, channel) linear: `ℝ^C → ℝ^C`, या two-layer linear (linear-activation-linear) जब DLinear-जैसा समानता चाहिए; positional encoding **नहीं** (canonical CycleNet minimalism) | 2-layer linear | — | depth ~ `(2–3)` stacked linear as MLP arm |\\n| Linear / projection head | final `ℝ^{H × C}` assembled by gather-on-cycle-index | ON | per-channel independent vs shared head — **Arm (f)** | `H ≤ 720`, सभी horizons एक head पर stacked |\\n| Instance normalization (channel-wise) | per-window mean/std on inputs only, inverse-applying on output (RevIN-style per-window affine) | **OFF (main run)** | **Arm (d)** in (h) | Main-run normalization = plain train stats per channel |\\n| Multi-scale CycleNet stacking | parallel cycles at `w_1, w_2, …`; predictions averaged/summed | **OFF (main run)** | **Arm (c)** in (h), **NICE-TO-HAVE** | अगर matrix overflow करे तो future-work में relegate; explicit assumption |\\n| Positional encoding | — | **OFF** | — | Canonical CycleNet में नहीं; assumptions में listed |\\n\\n### अंदर के design variables जिन्हें report करना है\\n\\n- `K` (residual decomposition depth) — main value = `K = w`; ablation में 1, 2, 4, w की grid पर।\\n- Period source `∈ {fixed w, FFT-autocorr-detected w}` — main = fixed; ablation arm (a)।\\n- Normalization ∈ {per-channel train stats, RevIN-like per-window affine} — main = train stats; arm (d)।\\n- Head ∈ {shared linear, per-channel independent linear} — arm (f)।\\n- Loss ∈ {MSE, MAE} — main = MSE; arm (e)।\\n\\n### Implementation assumptions vs well-supported facts\\n\\n- **Well-supported (high level)**: lookback को residual + period-index terms में decompose करना, अंतिम `w` samples पर forecasting block, और linear head — यह design सिद्धांतः canonical CycleNet description से मेल खाता है।\\n- **Assumptions (ऊपर default के रूप में लॉक किए गए)**: exact decomposition depth `K = w`, multi-block linear forecasting vs MLP, multi-scale stacking as optional only, RevIN opt-in via ablation arm only; positional encoding excluded; multi-channel joint prediction shared head as main।\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (c) Datasets and period assumptions — table\\n\\nDataset, अवधि, और data-access की स्थिति:\\n\\n| Dataset | Sampling | Canonical `w` | Periodicity interpretation | Data access (design runtime) |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| ETTh1 | hourly | `w = 24` | daily cycle (and `7×24 = 168` weekly secondary) | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\\n| ETTh2 | hourly | `w = 24` | daily | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\\n| ETTm1 | 15-min | `w = 96` | daily | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\\n| ETTm2 | 15-min | `w = 96` | daily | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\\n| Weather | 10-min | `w = 144` | daily | **download infeasible** (sandbox, no network) |\\n| Exchange | business-day | `w = 5` | weekly, business-day | **download infeasible** (sandbox, no network) |\\n| Electricity | hourly | `w = 24` | daily | **download infeasible** (sandbox, no network) |\\n| Traffic | hourly | `w = 24` | daily | **download infeasible** (sandbox, no network) |\\n| ILI | weekly | `w = 52` | yearly | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\\n\\n**Assumption (explicit)**: चूँकि `bubblewrap` sandbox में network disabled है, इसलिए Electricity / Traffic / Weather / Exchange के datasets **इस design phase में download नहीं किए जा सकते**। इसलिए इन datasets की सभी संख्याएँ design-time **specification** हैं, measured नहीं। यह एक **explicit execution prerequisite नोट** है — कोई measurement या runtime test इनके लिए नहीं किया गया।\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (d) Task formulation\\n\\n| Item | Specification |\\n|---|---|\\n| Input | `X ∈ ℝ^{L × C}`, sliding window with stride `= H` (training) `= H` (test, val) |\\n| Target | `Y ∈ ℝ^{H × C}` |\\n| Horizons `H` | ETT/Exchange/Weather/Electricity/Traffic → `{96, 192, 336, 720}`; ILI → `{24, 36, 48, 60}` |\\n| Lookback `L` | tuned over `{96, 192, 336, 720}` with constraint `L % w == 0`; selected best on validation MSE per `L`-grid; **report `L` per dataset** |\\n| Reporting variant | **Primary**: multivariate (all `C` channels jointly); **Secondary, labelled**: univariate on `OT` column for ETTh*/ETTm* families |\\n| Normalization (main) | per-channel mean/std from training split only; applied to inputs; targets inverse-transformed at evaluation |\\n| Normalization (RevIN ablation) | per-window mean/std on inputs, inverse on outputs; computed inside each window at train and inference |\\n| Padding of first `L` samples | **no padding**; forecast window generation starts from index `L` onwards — earlier samples simply not consumed |\\n| Splits — train/val/test | ETT `h`: 7:1:2; ETT `m`: 6:2:2; Electricity/Traffic: 70/10/20 (default; alternative 60/20/20 — declared at execution); Weather/Exchange: standard benchmark splits; ILI: standard splits; **strict time-disjoint, no rolling leak** |\\n| Rolling-leak safeguard | test windows generated with stride `= H` (no overlap); validation set also stride `= H` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (e) Training / optimization recipe\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Optimizer | Adam, `amsgrad=False` (default) |\\n| Weight decay | `∈ {1e-4, 1e-5}` (treat as small grid; default = `1e-4`) |\\n| Learning-rate schedule | cosine from peak `lr ∈ {1e-3, 5e-4, 1e-4}` to ~1% of peak over training; alternative one-cycle mentioned but **default = cosine** |\\n| Mini-batch size | `∈ {32, 64}` (baseline = 32) |\\n| Epochs | budget cap `∈ {100, 200}` (default cap = 100); early-stopping on validation MSE with patience = 10 epochs |\\n| Loss (backprop) | MSE on **standardized targets** |\\n| Loss (evaluation) | MSE and MAE on original scale; L1 backprop reported as ablation arm (e) |\\n| Gradient clipping | max-norm `1.0` |\\n| Seed protocol | `N_seeds = 3`; mean ± std across seeds reported for every `(dataset, horizon, metric)` |\\n| Threading | 24 CPU threads at process start; explicit `torch.set_num_threads(24)` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (f) Evaluation protocol and metrics\\n\\n**Primary metrics**:\\n- **MSE** on standardized targets (so backprop MSE = eval MSE up to scaling); used in all tables as primary.\\n- **MAE** on the original (un-standardized) scale; reported alongside MSE.\\n\\n**Protocol**:\\n- Multi-horizon **rolling evaluation** over **all test windows** with stride `= H` (no window overlap). For each window, predict `H` future steps; concatenate per-step metrics across windows to produce per-step (1…H) and aggregated per-horizon statistics.\\n- Aggregation: per-horizon MSE and MAE (matched to `H = {96, 192, 336, 720}`); plus unweighted mean across horizons (this is the scalar that enters comparison-vs-DLinear test).\\n\\n**Reporting granularity**:\\n- Per `(dataset, horizon, metric, seed)` and the per-row mean ± std across seeds (= 3).\\n- Primary table = multivariate; secondary table = univariate (OT column on ETT families only).\\n\\n**Reporting variant — univariate (ablation-by-convention only):**\\n- For ETTh*/ETTm*: univariate forecasts on the `OT` column alone, with same `H`, `L`, normalization protocol; reported in a separate, labelled table.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (g) Baselines\\n\\n| Baseline | Definition | Required | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `NAIVE-last` | `ŷ[t+1 : t+H] = x[t]` (last observed value broadcast over `H`) | **Yes — must-include** | Standard sanity floor |\\n| `NAIVE-seasonal-w` | `ŷ[t+h] = x[t+h−w]` (shifted to fall inside `[t−w+1, t]`) | **Yes — must-include** | Matches CycleNet's claim: period matters |\\n| `DLinear` | two parallel linear regressors on (i) moving-average trend `(K_avg)` and (ii) detrended series, summed; horizon produced by `Linear(L → H)` per channel (joint linear when multitask) | **Yes — must-include** | DLinear is the closest published reference; comparison floor for \\\"better than DLinear\\\" claims |\\n| Transformer-family reference | vanilla Transformer forecaster (input projection, positional encoding or RoPE-like, encoder-only, head = linear) | **Nice-to-have — discussion only** | यदि compute budget tight है तो explicitly \\\"out of scope, future work\\\" declare किया जाय; **कोई number fabricate नहीं किया जायगा** |\\n\\nOut-of-scope for this design: कोई भी Transformer जिसके लिए params tune करना या जटिल architectural choice आवश्यक हो (FEDformer / Informer आदि) — केवल discussion bullet तक सीमित।\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (h) Ablation matrix with priority\\n\\n| Priority | Arm | Variable | Levels | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| (a) | fixed `w` vs auto-detected `w` | period source | `{fixed canonical, FFT/autocorrelation peak}` | **Run on ETTh1 / ETTh2 / ETTm1 / ETTm2 / ILI** (5 datasets); default = fixed on the rest |\\n| (b) | residual decomposition depth `K` | `K` | `{1, 2, 4, K = w}` (with `K = w` being main) | **Run on every dataset** |\\n| (c) | multi-scale stacking | on/off | `{off, w₁=w, w₂=7w (when 7w ≤ L)}` | **NICE-TO-HAVE**; relegate to \\\"future-work\\\" paragraph if matrix overflows |\\n| (d) | normalization | per-channel train stats vs RevIN-like window-wise affine | `{train-stats, RevIN}` | **Run on every dataset** |\\n| (e) | loss | MSE vs MAE | `{MSE, MAE}` | **Sensitivity check, single horizon = 96 only**, to bound cost |\\n| (f) | head | shared linear vs per-channel independent linear | `{shared, per-channel}` | **Run on every dataset** |\\n\\n**Total size-bound (qualitative)**: main run base は `9 datasets × 4 horizons × 3 seeds` (specifications only). Priority ablations (a)+(b)+(d)+(f) multiply this by approximately the product of the per-arm grid sizes 2, 2, 2, 2 — order-of-magnitude low-to-mid hundreds of CPU-hours (qualitative, no fabricated figures). Sensitivity arm (e) at `H = 96` only adds a single-horizon extra layer.\\n\\n**Hard shrink protocol (explicit, if matrix overflows the budget once a CPU-hour ceiling is given)**:\\n1. **पहले** drop multi-scale arm (c) — relocate to future-work paragraph (matches NICE-TO-HAVE tag);\\n2. उसके बाद drop sensitivity arm (e) L1 — relocate to future-work;\\n3. अंतिम निर्णय — `N_seeds` को `3 → 2` घटाएँ only on low-priority arms; **हमेशा 3 seeds main run पर बने रहेंगे।**\\n\\n**Final hard-cap enforcement (assumptions explicitly listed)**:\\n- Data download bubblewrap में infeasible; किसी भी dataset का \\\"raw CSVs के साथ training\\\" execution के लिए spec की गई है, पर design deliverable में downloaded/measured नहीं है।\\n- Total ABI post-shrink target: **specification only — no fabricated number**; researcher द्वारा CPU-hour budget दिए जाने पर ये numbers finalized होंगे।\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (i) Controls (including leakage checks) and seed protocol\\n\\nUniversal controls applied to every compared model and every ablation:\\n\\n| Control | Description |\\n|---|---|\\n| Random seeds | fixed set `S = {s₁, s₂, s₃}`; `s₁` is the canonical seed; reproducible init everywhere (numpy, torch CPU) |\\n| Splits | train/val/test identical indices across all compared models |\\n| `L`, `H`, `w`, normalization statistics | identical across all models |\\n| Pipeline (cycle-indexed projection shape, head dimension) | identical constants |\\n| Loss / eval transform | identical |\\n\\n**Leakage checks** (explicit):\\n\\n| Check | How |\\n|---|---|\\n| Train/val/test time-disjoint | partitions strictly by index; **train before val before test** (no shuffling that mixes future into past) |\\n| No future in normalization | per-channel mean/std are computed **on training rows only**, then applied to all splits |\\n| No rolling leak between consecutive test windows | stride `= H`; forecast windows do not overlap on the input side; no shared input rows between two windows |\\n| No future in cycle-indexed projection | projection operates only on lookback `X`; targets `Y` are not indexed into the projection |\\n| No data leakage between ablation arms | each arm re-initializes from the same `s₁` (and `s₂, s₃`); no warm-start across arms |\\n\\n**Seed protocol**:\\n- Per `(model, dataset, horizon, metric)`: report `mean ± std` across `S`.\\n- Comparisons use **paired seeds** (same `sᵢ` for the model and its control).\\n- Failed seeds (`nan`, `inf`, abrupt divergence) explicitly enumerated; if a seed fails it is replaced and the failure logged — no silent replacement.\\n\\n**Necessary diagnostics (recorded per run, not used for selection bias)**:\\n- Train/val loss curves across epochs\\n- Gradient norm at each step (for sanity)\\n- Initial vs final MSE gap (to confirm the model trained at all)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (j) Analysis plan\\n\\n### Analyzed quantities\\n\\nFor each `(model M, dataset D, horizon H, seed s)`:\\n- multivariate MSE and MAE per horizon;\\n- unweighted mean across horizons (the scalar reported in the headline table);\\n- average across the 3 seeds (μ) and std (σ).\\n\\n### Pre-registered comparison rules\\n\\nA `CycleNet-...` configuration is declared **\\\"better than DLinear\\\"** if and only if:\\n\\n1. **Headline test**: at horizon `H`, multivariate MSE averaged across seeds — CycleNet μ < DLinear μ (numerically better, not equal).\\n2. **Sign consistency**: better-than-DLinear holds in all 3 seeds (no seed where CycleNet μ > DLinear μ at the same horizon).\\n3. **Magnitude reporting template** (qualitative rule): difference reported as `Δ = (μ_c − μ_D) ± √(σ_c² + σ_D²)`; the \\\"meaningfully better\\\" label is **not pre-fabricated** — an explicit reporting template is pre-registered and labelled on a per-case basis at execution time.\\n4. **Ablation correctness gate**: main run must pass the leakage checks (i) before any \\\"better than DLinear\\\" claim is logged; any leakage deviation voids the run.\\n5. **Univariate signal**: secondary table — univariate `OT`-only MSE on ETT families — must be consistent in direction with multivariate main table for the same seeds, or the configuration is flagged \\\"multivariate-eligible, univariate-ineligible\\\".\\n\\n### Headline table slots\\n\\n```\\nrows:     model ∈ {NAIVE-last, NAIVE-seasonal-w, DLinear, CycleNet-configurations}\\ncolumns:  (dataset, horizon) pairs\\ncells:    μ ± σ of multivariate MSE (and MAE in a parallel mirrored table)\\n```\\n\\nSecondary tables:\\n- univariate `OT` MSE for ETT families;\\n- normalization arm (RevIN vs train-stats) on every dataset;\\n- fixed-`w` vs auto-detected-`w` (a-priority subset);\\n- residual decomposition depth `K` sweep;\\n- loss sensitivity (MSE vs MAE) at `H = 96`.\\n\\n### Negative-result posture\\n\\nIf CycleNet does not beat DLinear on a given dataset/horizon, the design requires **honest reporting** with logs of train/val curves, normalization arm results, and an explicit note in the analysis why the result may have been obtained (e.g., small dataset like ILI may favor DLinear).\\n\\n### Out-of-scope analyses (future work)\\n\\n- Auto-`w` arm across all nine datasets (run-on-subset only by design);\\n- Multi-scale stacking (c);\\n- Transformer-family reference (g);\\n- comparison vs FEDformer / Informer (out of scope; no reference values cited as measured here).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (k) Feasibility / risks given CPU-only bubblewrap no-network runtime\\n\\n**Verified environment facts** (re-checked at this turn):\\n\\n| Fact | Observation |\\n|---|---|\\n| Runtime | `bubblewrap`, network disabled (per task contract) |\\n| Python | 3.12.3 |\\n| Preinstalled numerical libs | **none** (numpy import fails) |\\n| pip3 | system `/usr/bin/pip3` (v24.0) present, but no project deps preinstalled |\\n| CPU threads | 24 |\\n| Memory | ~125 GiB total, ~96 GiB available |\\n| GPU | none |\\n| Workspace | `/workspace` contains `task.json` only |\\n\\n**Stated execution prerequisites** (NOT part of the design deliverable):\\n\\n| Prereq | What | Why |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `pip install numpy torch --index-url ...` (CPU build) | numerical stack | absent today |\\n| `pip install pandas` | CSV/HDF5 IO | absent today |\\n| Dataset access | CSVs at canonical paths or local cache; **downloads infeasible** under bubblewrap | runtime constraint |\\n\\n**CPU-only feasibility (qualitative, no fabricated numbers)**:\\n\\n- CycleNet का core mostly matmul + integer indexing है, इसलिए depth नहीं, बल्कि `L`, `H`, batch, dataset size dominate करते हैं।\\n- For the small benchmark sizes typical of the ETTh*/ETTm*/ILI dataset subset (sub-millions of rows), total main run (without ablations) is order-of-magnitude low tens of CPU-hours on 24 threads — this is a **qualitative estimate** (no per-epoch number is fabricated).\\n- For the full matrix with priority arms (a)+(b)+(d)+(f), order-of-magnitude low-to-mid hundreds of CPU-hours; shrink protocol above applies if a research budget is given.\\n- For Electricity/Traffic/Weather/Exchange: dataset sizes are larger; any unconstrained run could push into the multiple-of-hundreds range; **explicit assumption** — these are listed as design specifications only, **unless** the user provisions data locally first.\\n\\n**Risk register**:\\n\\n| Risk | Mitigation in design |\\n|---|---|\\n| Network disabled — dataset download infeasible | explicit prerequisite listing; **all per-dataset numbers in this design are specification, not measurement** |\\n| No preinstalled numerical libs | execution prerequisite (`pip install`) listed; design does not assume they are available |\\n| Compute overflow on full ablation matrix | shrink protocol in (h); main run protects first |\\n| Numerical instability (inst-norm vs train-stats mismatch) | gradient-clip = 1.0; seed protocol; RevIN isolated to a single ablation arm |\\n| Cycle-index projection misalignment when `L % w != 0` | constraint `L % w == 0` enforced in `L` grid |\\n| Per-channel independent head overparameterization on small datasets (ILI) | arm (f) reported only, not in headline |\\n| Variance masking real differences | mean ± std across 3 seeds reported; sign-consistency gate |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (l) Explicit \\\"not run\\\" statement\\n\\nयह दस्तावेज़ **केवल design** है। किसी भी dataset के लिए **कोई training execute नहीं हुई है**, **कोई MSE/MAE measured नहीं किया गया है**, और **कोई baseline running नहीं हुई है**। सभी संख्याएँ, hyperparameter ranges, `L`/`H` grids, और per-dataset `w` values — सब **specification** हैं, **measured नहीं**। \\\"CycleNet beats DLinear\\\" जैसा कोई claim इस deliverable में **नहीं** किया गया है; comparison rules purely pre-registered हैं और apply किए जायेंगे यदि/जब execution हो।\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Assumption ledger (research document, beyond the resolved defaults)\\n\\nOne running prose, semicolon-separated:\\nCycle-indexed gather numerics float32 में पर्याप्त assume किए गए हैं — fp16/bf16 considered नहीं किया गया क्योंकि GPU नहीं है; 24 threads पर degree-of-parallelism effective माना गया है (छोटे linear layer batch में CPU contention से प्रभावित नहीं), wider grid पर re-evaluate किया जायगा; standard benchmark splits (ETT 7:1:2 / 6:2:2, Elec/Traffic 70/10/20) reproducing-published conditions के लिए काफ़ी माने गए हैं, CSV version mismatch पर anchor-by-date protocol पर host से confirmation आवश्यक है; per-channel independent vs shared head arm (f) एक diagnostic है, headline नहीं; FFT/autocorrelation-based period detection arm (a) की implementation detail को FFT magnitude peak (≥ 0.5 × Nyquist) या ACF lag-`w` peak (≥ 0.5 of dominant lag) तक restricted किया गया है, exact scipy/numpy FFT signature पर locked नहीं है।\\n\\n### Open items (next-turn decision if user requests)\\n\\nOne running prose, semicolon-separated:\\nTransformer-family reference formally listed baseline में है या \\\"future work\\\" में relegate या drop — current default = future work, पर lock नहीं हुआ; CPU-hour budget ceiling आने पर shrink protocol trigger threshold re-evaluate किया जायगा; headline matrix में Electricity/Traffic की retention का निर्णय execution से पहले local cache provisioning पर depend करता है।\",\"evidence\":\"Workspace contents under /workspace: only task.json is present (≈395 bytes). `track.md` is the documents.track.md field inside task.json with the single-line content 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.' Verified runtime: bubblewrap (no network); python3 --version → Python 3.12.3; `import numpy` fails with ModuleNotFoundError; system pip3 v24.0 exists but no project deps installed; nproc → 24; free -h → ~125 GiB RAM total, ~96 GiB available; no GPU. All numerical claims in the design are specifications only — no execution occurred, no measure taken, no fabricated per-epoch times reported.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"One running prose, semicolon-separated: Data access for Electricity/Traffic/Weather/Exchange is infeasible in bubblewrap so per-dataset numbers in this design are specification, not measurement.\"}}}}}}],\"uncertainties\":[\"One running prose, semicolon-separated: CPU-hour budget ceiling is not yet given, shrink protocol trigger threshold will be re-evaluated once budget is provided; Transformer-family reference status (formal baseline vs future work vs dropped) is not yet locked; whether Electricity/Traffic should remain in the headline matrix if a local cache path is not provisioned before execution is not yet decided.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-c7764d7e-3f10-4b5d-9c79-586b598d72c9", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 21}
