{"id": "3946d38f-6f30-42c8-89a3-90f703e8a063", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T19:47:58.903748", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "c1e7a174-e0af-4e50-b99b-c820d2cd013f", "action": {"stage": "result", "answer": "# CycleNet-style periodic time-series forecasting — experiment design\n\n> डिज़ाइन-मात्र दस्तावेज़। Execution नहीं हुआ है। सभी संख्याएँ specification हैं, मापी गई मान नहीं।\n> Runtime: bubblewrap, network disabled, Python 3.12.3, no preinstalled numerical libraries (numpy भी नहीं), 24 CPU threads, no GPU.\n> Workspace `/workspace` में केवल `task.json` है (≈395 bytes); `track.md` फ़ाइल磁盘 पर नहीं है — `task.json` का `documents.track.md` फ़ील्ड एक-पंक्ति वाला design-only नोट है।\n\n---\n\n## (a) Research question (पुनः-कथन)\n\nहम यह जाँचना चाहते हैं कि CycleNet-शैली की residual-cycle forecasting architecture का उपयोग करके periodic structure वाले multivariate time-series पर, पूर्व-निर्धारित अवधि w के साथ (canonical / dataset-known) और सामान्य benchmark datasets पर setting, DLinear जैसे linear baselines से क्या तुलना में MSE / MAE मान आते हैं और कौन-से अवयव (residual decomposition depth, fixed vs auto-detected w, RevIN-style normalization, multi-scale stacking, loss choice) प्रभाव डालते हैं।\n\nQuestion को operationally testable बनाने के लिए नीचे pre-registered comparison rule (अनुभाग (j)) दिया गया है — \"better than DLinear\" का दावा तभी होगा जब (i) average across N_seeds=3 पर अंतर >0 और (ii) sign across seeds consistent हो।\n\n---\n\n## (b) CycleNet component specification\n\n### मूल ढाँचा (canonical high-level, well-supported at high level only)\n\nदिया हुआ lookback X ∈ R^{L x C} जहाँ L = lookback, C = number of channels, और एक चुनी हुई canonical अवधि w (नीचे (c) की table के अनुसार)।\n\nमूल घटक (Block diagram — specification, not measured):\n\n```\nX ∈ R^{L x C}\n   |\n   |--[Residual extraction]---- r_0 ∈ R^{w x C}        (averaged over floor(L/w) whole cycles; take last w)\n   |\n   |--[Cycle-indexed projection, K terms]---\n   |      for k in {0, 1, …, K-1}:   r_k ∈ R^{w x C}    (samples whose (t mod w) == k)\n   |      sum(CycleIndexDecomp) restores L samples per channel\n   |\n   |--[Residual cycle-forecasting block, per k]\n   |      linear / small MLP on r_k[-w:] → o_k ∈ R^{H x C}    (last w samples पर apply)\n   |\n   |--[Invert cycle-indexed projection]---\n   |      for k in {0,1,…,H-1}: assign each target step h to offset index (h mod w), gathering o_{k}[h]\n   |\n   |--[Linear / projection head]--→ Ŷ ∈ R^{H x C}\n```\n\n### घटक-दर-घटक विनिर्देश\n\n| घटक | Specification | Default | Optional arm | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Residual extraction (single) | epoch-wise averaging of full-cycle subsequences; last w rows retained | ON | — | Baseline depth; canonical \"1-cycle residual\" |\n| Multi-cycle residual decomposition | ऊपर जैसा, पर K = w पूर्ण cycle indices | OFF (main run) | Arm (b) in (h) | Specification says K dim पर ablate |\n| Cycle-indexed projection | (t mod w) द्वारा index, चैनल-वार | ON | — | Implementation note: efficient reshape [B, L//w, w, C] indexed operation |\n| Forecasting block (residual cycle-forecasting) | per-(index, channel) linear: R^C → R^C, या two-layer linear (linear-activation-linear) जब DLinear-जैसा समानता चाहिए; positional encoding नहीं (canonical CycleNet minimalism) | 2-layer linear | — | depth ~ (2–3) stacked linear as MLP arm |\n| Linear / projection head | final R^{H x C} assembled by gather-on-cycle-index | ON | per-channel independent vs shared head — Arm (f) | H ≤ 720, सभी horizons एक head पर stacked |\n| Instance normalization (channel-wise) | per-window mean/std on inputs only, inverse-applying on output (RevIN-style per-window affine) | OFF (main run) | Arm (d) in (h) | Main-run normalization = plain train stats per channel |\n| Multi-scale CycleNet stacking | parallel cycles at w_1, w_2, …; predictions averaged/summed | OFF (main run) | Arm (c) in (h), NICE-TO-HAVE | अगर matrix overflow करे तो future-work में relegate; explicit assumption |\n| Positional encoding | — | OFF | — | Canonical CycleNet में नहीं |\n\n### अंदर के design variables जिन्हें report करना है\n\n- K (residual decomposition depth) — main value = K = w; ablation में 1, 2, 4, w की grid पर।\n- Period source ∈ {fixed w, FFT-autocorr-detected w} — main = fixed; ablation arm (a)।\n- Normalization ∈ {per-channel train stats, RevIN-like per-window affine} — main = train stats; arm (d)।\n- Head ∈ {shared linear, per-channel independent linear} — arm (f)।\n- Loss ∈ {MSE, MAE} — main = MSE; arm (e)।\n\n### Implementation assumptions vs well-supported facts\n\n- Well-supported (high level): lookback को residual + period-index terms में decompose करना, अंतिम w samples पर forecasting block, और linear head — यह design सिद्धांतः canonical CycleNet description से मेल खाता है।\n- Assumptions (ऊपर default के रूप में लॉक किए गए): exact decomposition depth K = w, multi-block linear forecasting vs MLP, multi-scale stacking as optional only, RevIN opt-in via ablation arm only; positional encoding excluded; multi-channel joint prediction shared head as main।\n\n---\n\n## (c) Datasets and period assumptions — table\n\n| Dataset | Sampling | Canonical w | Periodicity interpretation | Data access (design runtime) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ETTh1 | hourly | w = 24 | daily cycle (and 7×24 = 168 weekly secondary) | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\n| ETTh2 | hourly | w = 24 | daily | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\n| ETTm1 | 15-min | w = 96 | daily | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\n| ETTm2 | 15-min | w = 96 | daily | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\n| Weather | 10-min | w = 144 | daily | download infeasible (sandbox, no network) |\n| Exchange | business-day | w = 5 | weekly, business-day | download infeasible (sandbox, no network) |\n| Electricity | hourly | w = 24 | daily | download infeasible (sandbox, no network) |\n| Traffic | hourly | w = 24 | daily | download infeasible (sandbox, no network) |\n| ILI | weekly | w = 52 | yearly | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\n\nAssumption (explicit): चूँकि bubblewrap sandbox में network disabled है, इसलिए Electricity / Traffic / Weather / Exchange के datasets इस design phase में download नहीं किए जा सकते। इन datasets की सभी संख्याएँ design-time specification हैं, measured नहीं। यह explicit execution prerequisite नोट है — कोई measurement या runtime test इनके लिए नहीं किया गया।\n\n---\n\n## (d) Task formulation\n\n| Item | Specification |\n|---|---|\n| Input | X ∈ R^{L x C}, sliding window with stride = H (training) = H (test, val) |\n| Target | Y ∈ R^{H x C} |\n| Horizons H | ETT/Exchange/Weather/Electricity/Traffic → {96, 192, 336, 720}; ILI → {24, 36, 48, 60} |\n| Lookback L | tuned over {96, 192, 336, 720} with constraint L % w == 0; selected best on validation MSE per L-grid; report L per dataset |\n| Reporting variant | Primary: multivariate (all C channels jointly); Secondary, labelled: univariate on OT column for ETTh*/ETTm* families |\n| Normalization (main) | per-channel mean/std from training split only; applied to inputs; targets inverse-transformed at evaluation |\n| Normalization (RevIN ablation) | per-window mean/std on inputs, inverse on outputs; computed inside each window at train and inference |\n| Padding of first L samples | no padding; forecast window generation starts from index L onwards — earlier samples simply not consumed |\n| Splits — train/val/test | ETT h: 7:1:2; ETT m: 6:2:2; Electricity/Traffic: 70/10/20 (default; alternative 60/20/20 declared at execution); Weather/Exchange: standard benchmark splits; ILI: standard splits; strict time-disjoint, no rolling leak |\n| Rolling-leak safeguard | test windows generated with stride = H (no overlap); validation set also stride = H |\n\n---\n\n## (e) Training / optimization recipe\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Optimizer | Adam, amsgrad=False (default) |\n| Weight decay | ∈ {1e-4, 1e-5} (treat as small grid; default = 1e-4) |\n| Learning-rate schedule | cosine from peak lr ∈ {1e-3, 5e-4, 1e-4} to ~1% of peak over training; alternative one-cycle mentioned but default = cosine |\n| Mini-batch size | ∈ {32, 64} (baseline = 32) |\n| Epochs | budget cap ∈ {100, 200} (default cap = 100); early-stopping on validation MSE with patience = 10 epochs |\n| Loss (backprop) | MSE on standardized targets |\n| Loss (evaluation) | MSE and MAE on original scale; L1 backprop reported as ablation arm (e) |\n| Gradient clipping | max-norm 1.0 |\n| Seed protocol | N_seeds = 3; mean ± std across seeds reported for every (dataset, horizon, metric) |\n| Threading | 24 CPU threads at process start; explicit torch.set_num_threads(24) |\n\n---\n\n## (f) Evaluation protocol and metrics\n\nPrimary metrics:\n- MSE on standardized targets (so backprop MSE = eval MSE up to scaling); used in all tables as primary.\n- MAE on the original (un-standardized) scale; reported alongside MSE.\n\nProtocol:\n- Multi-horizon rolling evaluation over all test windows with stride = H (no window overlap). For each window, predict H future steps; concatenate per-step metrics across windows to produce per-step (1…H) and aggregated per-horizon statistics.\n- Aggregation: per-horizon MSE and MAE (matched to H = {96, 192, 336, 720}); plus unweighted mean across horizons (the scalar that enters comparison-vs-DLinear test).\n\nReporting granularity:\n- Per (dataset, horizon, metric, seed) and the per-row mean ± std across seeds (= 3).\n- Primary table = multivariate; secondary table = univariate (OT column on ETT families only).\n\nReporting variant — univariate (ablation-by-convention only):\n- For ETTh*/ETTm*: univariate forecasts on the OT column alone, with same H, L, normalization protocol; reported in a separate, labelled table.\n\n---\n\n## (g) Baselines\n\n| Baseline | Definition | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NAIVE-last | ŷ[t+1:t+H] = x[t] (last observed value broadcast over H) | Yes — must-include | Standard sanity floor |\n| NAIVE-seasonal-w | ŷ[t+h] = x[t+h-w] (shifted to fall inside [t-w+1, t]) | Yes — must-include | Matches CycleNet's claim: period matters |\n| DLinear | two parallel linear regressors on (i) moving-average trend (K_avg) and (ii) detrended series, summed; horizon produced by Linear(L → H) per channel (joint linear when multitask) | Yes — must-include | DLinear is the closest published reference; comparison floor for \"better than DLinear\" claims |\n| Transformer-family reference | vanilla Transformer forecaster (input projection, positional encoding or RoPE-like, encoder-only, head = linear) | Nice-to-have — discussion only | यदि compute budget tight है तो explicitly \"out of scope, future work\" declare किया जाय; कोई number fabricate नहीं किया जायगा |\n\nOut-of-scope for this design: कोई भी Transformer जिसके लिए params tune करना या जटिल architectural choice आवश्यक हो (FEDformer / Informer आदि) — केवल discussion bullet तक सीमित।\n\n---\n\n## (h) Ablation matrix with priority\n\n| Priority | Arm | Variable | Levels | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (a) | fixed w vs auto-detected w | period source | {fixed canonical, FFT/autocorrelation peak} | Run on ETTh1 / ETTh2 / ETTm1 / ETTm2 / ILI (5 datasets); default = fixed on the rest |\n| (b) | residual decomposition depth K | K | {1, 2, 4, K = w} (with K = w being main) | Run on every dataset |\n| (c) | multi-scale stacking | on/off | {off, w1=w, w2=7w (when 7w ≤ L)} | NICE-TO-HAVE; relegate to \"future-work\" paragraph if matrix overflows |\n| (d) | normalization | per-channel train stats vs RevIN-like window-wise affine | {train-stats, RevIN} | Run on every dataset |\n| (e) | loss | MSE vs MAE | {MSE, MAE} | Sensitivity check, single horizon = 96 only, to bound cost |\n| (f) | head | shared linear vs per-channel independent linear | {shared, per-channel} | Run on every dataset |\n\nTotal size-bound (qualitative): main run base = 9 datasets × 4 horizons × 3 seeds (specifications only). Priority ablations (a)+(b)+(d)+(f) multiply this by approximately the product of per-arm grid sizes 2, 2, 2, 2 — order-of-magnitude low-to-mid hundreds of CPU-hours (qualitative, no fabricated figures). Sensitivity arm (e) at H = 96 only adds a single-horizon extra layer.\n\nHard shrink protocol (explicit, if matrix overflows the budget once a CPU-hour ceiling is given):\n1. पहले drop multi-scale arm (c) — relocate to future-work paragraph (matches NICE-TO-HAVE tag).\n2. उसके बाद drop sensitivity arm (e) L1 — relocate to future-work.\n3. अंतिम निर्णय — N_seeds को 3 → 2 घटाएँ only on low-priority arms; हमेशा 3 seeds main run पर बने रहेंगे।\n\nFinal hard-cap enforcement (assumptions explicitly listed):\n- Data download bubblewrap में infeasible; किसी भी dataset का raw CSVs के साथ training execution के लिए spec की गई है, पर design deliverable में downloaded/measured नहीं है।\n- Total ABI post-shrink target: specification only — no fabricated number; researcher द्वारा CPU-hour budget दिए जाने पर ये numbers finalized होंगे।\n\n---\n\n## (i) Controls (including leakage checks) and seed protocol\n\nUniversal controls applied to every compared model and every ablation:\n\n| Control | Description |\n|---|---|\n| Random seeds | fixed set S = {s1, s2, s3}; s1 is the canonical seed; reproducible init everywhere (numpy, torch CPU) |\n| Splits | train/val/test identical indices across all compared models |\n| L, H, w, normalization statistics | identical across all models |\n| Pipeline (cycle-indexed projection shape, head dimension) | identical constants |\n| Loss / eval transform | identical |\n\nLeakage checks (explicit):\n\n| Check | How |\n|---|---|\n| Train/val/test time-disjoint | partitions strictly by index; train before val before test (no shuffling that mixes future into past) |\n| No future in normalization | per-channel mean/std are computed on training rows only, then applied to all splits |\n| No rolling leak between consecutive test windows | stride = H; forecast windows do not overlap on the input side; no shared input rows between two windows |\n| No future in cycle-indexed projection | projection operates only on lookback X; targets Y are not indexed into the projection |\n| No data leakage between ablation arms | each arm re-initializes from the same s1 (and s2, s3); no warm-start across arms |\n\nSeed protocol:\n- Per (model, dataset, horizon, metric): report mean ± std across S.\n- Comparisons use paired seeds (same si for the model and its control).\n- Failed seeds (nan, inf, abrupt divergence) explicitly enumerated; if a seed fails it is replaced and the failure logged — no silent replacement.\n\nNecessary diagnostics (recorded per run, not used for selection bias):\n- Train/val loss curves across epochs.\n- Gradient norm at each step (for sanity).\n- Initial vs final MSE gap (to confirm the model trained at all).\n\n---\n\n## (j) Analysis plan\n\n### Analyzed quantities\n\nFor each (model M, dataset D, horizon H, seed s):\n- multivariate MSE and MAE per horizon;\n- unweighted mean across horizons (the scalar reported in the headline table);\n- average across the 3 seeds (μ) and std (σ).\n\n### Pre-registered comparison rules\n\nA CycleNet-... configuration is declared \"better than DLinear\" if and only if:\n\n1. Headline test: at horizon H, multivariate MSE averaged across seeds — CycleNet μ < DLinear μ (numerically better, not equal).\n2. Sign consistency: better-than-DLinear holds in all 3 seeds (no seed where CycleNet μ > DLinear μ at the same horizon).\n3. Magnitude reporting template (qualitative rule): difference reported as Δ = (μ_c − μ_D) ± √(σ_c^2 + σ_D^2); the \"meaningfully better\" label is not pre-fabricated — an explicit reporting template is pre-registered and labelled on a per-case basis at execution time.\n4. Ablation correctness gate: main run must pass the leakage checks (i) before any \"better than DLinear\" claim is logged; any leakage deviation voids the run.\n5. Univariate signal: secondary table — univariate OT-only MSE on ETT families — must be consistent in direction with multivariate main table for the same seeds, or the configuration is flagged \"multivariate-eligible, univariate-ineligible\".\n\n### Headline table slots\n\n```\nrows:     model ∈ {NAIVE-last, NAIVE-seasonal-w, DLinear, CycleNet-configurations}\ncolumns:  (dataset, horizon) pairs\ncells:    μ ± σ of multivariate MSE (and MAE in a parallel mirrored table)\n```\n\nSecondary tables:\n- univariate OT MSE for ETT families;\n- normalization arm (RevIN vs train-stats) on every dataset;\n- fixed-w vs auto-detected-w (a-priority subset);\n- residual decomposition depth K sweep;\n- loss sensitivity (MSE vs MAE) at H = 96.\n\n### Negative-result posture\n\nIf CycleNet does not beat DLinear on a given dataset/horizon, the design requires honest reporting with logs of train/val curves, normalization arm results, and an explicit note in the analysis why the result may have been obtained (e.g., small dataset like ILI may favor DLinear).\n\n### Out-of-scope analyses (future work)\n\n- Auto-w arm across all nine datasets (run-on-subset only by design);\n- Multi-scale stacking (c);\n- Transformer-family reference (g);\n- comparison vs FEDformer / Informer (out of scope; no reference values cited as measured here).\n\n---\n\n## (k) Feasibility / risks given CPU-only bubblewrap no-network runtime\n\nVerified environment facts (re-checked at this turn):\n\n| Fact | Observation |\n|---|---|\n| Runtime | bubblewrap, network disabled (per task contract) |\n| Python | 3.12.3 |\n| Preinstalled numerical libs | none (numpy import fails) |\n| pip3 | system /usr/bin/pip3 (v24.0) present, but no project deps preinstalled |\n| CPU threads | 24 |\n| Memory | ~125 GiB total, ~96 GiB available |\n| GPU | none |\n| Workspace | /workspace contains task.json only |\n\nStated execution prerequisites (NOT part of the design deliverable):\n\n| Prereq | What | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| pip install numpy torch --index-url ... (CPU build) | numerical stack | absent today |\n| pip install pandas | CSV/HDF5 IO | absent today |\n| Dataset access | CSVs at canonical paths or local cache; downloads infeasible under bubblewrap | runtime constraint |\n\nCPU-only feasibility (qualitative, no fabricated numbers):\n- CycleNet का core mostly matmul + integer indexing है, इसलिए depth नहीं, बल्कि L, H, batch, dataset size dominate करते हैं।\n- For the small benchmark sizes typical of the ETTh*/ETTm*/ILI dataset subset (sub-millions of rows), total main run (without ablations) is order-of-magnitude low tens of CPU-hours on 24 threads — this is a qualitative estimate (no per-epoch number is fabricated).\n- For the full matrix with priority arms (a)+(b)+(d)+(f), order-of-magnitude low-to-mid hundreds of CPU-hours; shrink protocol above applies if a research budget is given.\n- For Electricity/Traffic/Weather/Exchange: dataset sizes are larger; any unconstrained run could push into the multiple-of-hundreds range; explicit assumption — these are listed as design specifications only, unless the user provisions data locally first.\n\nRisk register:\n\n| Risk | Mitigation in design |\n|---|---|\n| Network disabled — dataset download infeasible | explicit prerequisite listing; all per-dataset numbers in this design are specification, not measurement |\n| No preinstalled numerical libs | execution prerequisite (pip install) listed; design does not assume they are available |\n| Compute overflow on full ablation matrix | shrink protocol in (h); main run protects first |\n| Numerical instability (inst-norm vs train-stats mismatch) | gradient-clip = 1.0; seed protocol; RevIN isolated to a single ablation arm |\n| Cycle-index projection misalignment when L % w != 0 | constraint L % w == 0 enforced in L grid |\n| Per-channel independent head overparameterization on small datasets (ILI) | arm (f) reported only, not in headline |\n| Variance masking real differences | mean ± std across 3 seeds reported; sign-consistency gate |\n\n---\n\n## (l) Explicit \"not run\" statement\n\nयह दस्तावेज़ केवल design है। किसी भी dataset के लिए कोई training execute नहीं हुई है, कोई MSE/MAE measured नहीं किया गया है, और कोई baseline running नहीं हुई है। सभी संख्याएँ, hyperparameter ranges, L/H grids, और per-dataset w values — सब specification हैं, measured नहीं। \"CycleNet beats DLinear\" जैसा कोई claim इस deliverable में नहीं किया गया है; comparison rules purely pre-registered हैं और apply किए जायेंगे यदि/जब execution हो।\n\n---\n\n### Assumption ledger (research document, beyond the resolved defaults)\n\nCycle-indexed gather numerics float32 में पर्याप्त assume किए गए हैं; 24 CPU threads पर degree-of-parallelism effective माना गया है (छोटे linear layer batch में CPU contention से प्रभावित नहीं), wider grid पर re-evaluate किया जायगा; standard benchmark splits (ETT 7:1:2 / 6:2:2, Electricity/Traffic 70/10/20) reproducing-published conditions के लिए काफ़ी माने गए हैं, CSV version mismatch पर anchor-by-date protocol पर host से confirmation आवश्यक है; per-channel independent vs shared head arm (f) एक diagnostic है, headline नहीं; FFT/autocorrelation-based period detection arm (a) की implementation detail को FFT magnitude peak (≥ 0.5 × Nyquist) या ACF lag-w peak (≥ 0.5 of dominant lag) तक restricted किया गया है, exact scipy/numpy FFT signature पर locked नहीं है।\n\n### Open items (next-turn decision if user requests)\n\nTransformer-family reference formally listed baseline में है या future work में relegate या drop — current default = future work, पर lock नहीं हुआ; CPU-hour budget ceiling आने पर shrink protocol trigger threshold re-evaluate किया जायगा; headline matrix में Electricity/Traffic की retention का निर्णय execution से पहले local cache provisioning पर depend करता है।", "evidence": "Workspace contents under /workspace: only task.json is present (≈395 bytes). `track.md` is the documents.track.md field inside task.json with the single-line content 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.' Verified runtime: bubblewrap (no network); python3 --version → Python 3.12.3; `import numpy` fails with ModuleNotFoundError; system pip3 v24.0 exists but no project deps installed; nproc → 24; free -h → ~125 GiB RAM total, ~96 GiB available; no GPU. All numerical claims in the design are specifications only — no execution occurred, no measure taken, no fabricated per-epoch times reported.", "assumptions": ["Data access for Electricity/Traffic/Weather/Exchange is infeasible in bubblewrap, so per-dataset numbers in this design are specification, not measurement.</item>\n<item>Datasets ETTh*/ETTm*/ILI are listed as design-time specifications pending execution-time data access (CSV/HDF5 at canonical paths).</item>\n<item>Cycle-indexed projection implementation assumed to be efficient via reshape [B, L//w, w, C] and gather; exact code deferred to execution.</item>\n<item>CycleNet canonical high-level idea (residual + period-indexed decomposition, forecast on last w, linear head) is taken as well-supported; depth K, multi-scale stacking opt-in, RevIN opt-in, no positional encoding are design choices, not source-confirmed facts.</item>\n<item>Standard benchmark splits (ETT 7:1:2 / 6:2:2, Electricity/Traffic 70/10/20) are assumed to be the canonical splits; CSV version mismatch requires anchor-by-date confirmation at execution.</item>\n<item>CPU-only feasibility estimate is qualitative (low-tens to low-hundreds of CPU-hours) — no fabricated per-epoch or per-run numbers.</item>\n<item>Float32 numerics are sufficient for cycle-indexed gather; fp16/bf16 not considered because GPU is absent.</item>"], "uncertainties": ["CPU-hour budget ceiling is not yet given; the shrink-protocol trigger threshold in (h) will be re-evaluated once a budget is provided.</item>\n<item>Transformer-family reference status (formal baseline vs future work vs dropped) is not yet locked.</item>\n<item>Whether Electricity/Traffic should remain in the headline matrix if a local cache path is not provisioned before execution is not yet decided.</item>"], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-447f5cda-50c7-4e79-9a2f-71531d71a6ca", "tool_call": {"id": "call-447f5cda-50c7-4e79-9a2f-71531d71a6ca", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Submit full CycleNet experiment design (Hindi narrative, English technical)\", \"stage\": \"result\", \"answer\": \"# CycleNet-style periodic time-series forecasting \\u2014 experiment design\\n\\n> \\u0921\\u093f\\u091c\\u093c\\u093e\\u0907\\u0928-\\u092e\\u093e\\u0924\\u094d\\u0930 \\u0926\\u0938\\u094d\\u0924\\u093e\\u0935\\u0947\\u091c\\u093c\\u0964 Execution \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0939\\u0941\\u0906 \\u0939\\u0948\\u0964 \\u0938\\u092d\\u0940 \\u0938\\u0902\\u0916\\u094d\\u092f\\u093e\\u090f\\u0901 specification \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902, \\u092e\\u093e\\u092a\\u0940 \\u0917\\u0908 \\u092e\\u093e\\u0928 \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902\\u0964\\n> Runtime: bubblewrap, network disabled, Python 3.12.3, no preinstalled numerical libraries (numpy \\u092d\\u0940 \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902), 24 CPU threads, no GPU.\\n> Workspace `/workspace` \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 \\u0915\\u0947\\u0935\\u0932 `task.json` \\u0939\\u0948 (\\u2248395 bytes); `track.md` \\u092b\\u093c\\u093e\\u0907\\u0932\\u78c1\\u76d8 \\u092a\\u0930 \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0939\\u0948 \\u2014 `task.json` \\u0915\\u093e `documents.track.md` \\u092b\\u093c\\u0940\\u0932\\u094d\\u0921 \\u090f\\u0915-\\u092a\\u0902\\u0915\\u094d\\u0924\\u093f \\u0935\\u093e\\u0932\\u093e design-only \\u0928\\u094b\\u091f \\u0939\\u0948\\u0964\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (a) Research question (\\u092a\\u0941\\u0928\\u0903-\\u0915\\u0925\\u0928)\\n\\n\\u0939\\u092e \\u092f\\u0939 \\u091c\\u093e\\u0901\\u091a\\u0928\\u093e \\u091a\\u093e\\u0939\\u0924\\u0947 \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902 \\u0915\\u093f CycleNet-\\u0936\\u0948\\u0932\\u0940 \\u0915\\u0940 residual-cycle forecasting architecture \\u0915\\u093e \\u0909\\u092a\\u092f\\u094b\\u0917 \\u0915\\u0930\\u0915\\u0947 periodic structure \\u0935\\u093e\\u0932\\u0947 multivariate time-series \\u092a\\u0930, \\u092a\\u0942\\u0930\\u094d\\u0935-\\u0928\\u093f\\u0930\\u094d\\u0927\\u093e\\u0930\\u093f\\u0924 \\u0905\\u0935\\u0927\\u093f w \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0938\\u093e\\u0925 (canonical / dataset-known) \\u0914\\u0930 \\u0938\\u093e\\u092e\\u093e\\u0928\\u094d\\u092f benchmark datasets \\u092a\\u0930 setting, DLinear \\u091c\\u0948\\u0938\\u0947 linear baselines \\u0938\\u0947 \\u0915\\u094d\\u092f\\u093e \\u0924\\u0941\\u0932\\u0928\\u093e \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 MSE / MAE \\u092e\\u093e\\u0928 \\u0906\\u0924\\u0947 \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902 \\u0914\\u0930 \\u0915\\u094c\\u0928-\\u0938\\u0947 \\u0905\\u0935\\u092f\\u0935 (residual decomposition depth, fixed vs auto-detected w, RevIN-style normalization, multi-scale stacking, loss choice) \\u092a\\u094d\\u0930\\u092d\\u093e\\u0935 \\u0921\\u093e\\u0932\\u0924\\u0947 \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902\\u0964\\n\\nQuestion \\u0915\\u094b operationally testable \\u092c\\u0928\\u093e\\u0928\\u0947 \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0932\\u093f\\u090f \\u0928\\u0940\\u091a\\u0947 pre-registered comparison rule (\\u0905\\u0928\\u0941\\u092d\\u093e\\u0917 (j)) \\u0926\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u0917\\u092f\\u093e \\u0939\\u0948 \\u2014 \\\"better than DLinear\\\" \\u0915\\u093e \\u0926\\u093e\\u0935\\u093e \\u0924\\u092d\\u0940 \\u0939\\u094b\\u0917\\u093e \\u091c\\u092c (i) average across N_seeds=3 \\u092a\\u0930 \\u0905\\u0902\\u0924\\u0930 >0 \\u0914\\u0930 (ii) sign across seeds consistent \\u0939\\u094b\\u0964\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (b) CycleNet component specification\\n\\n### \\u092e\\u0942\\u0932 \\u0922\\u093e\\u0901\\u091a\\u093e (canonical high-level, well-supported at high level only)\\n\\n\\u0926\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u0939\\u0941\\u0906 lookback X \\u2208 R^{L x C} \\u091c\\u0939\\u093e\\u0901 L = lookback, C = number of channels, \\u0914\\u0930 \\u090f\\u0915 \\u091a\\u0941\\u0928\\u0940 \\u0939\\u0941\\u0908 canonical \\u0905\\u0935\\u0927\\u093f w (\\u0928\\u0940\\u091a\\u0947 (c) \\u0915\\u0940 table \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0905\\u0928\\u0941\\u0938\\u093e\\u0930)\\u0964\\n\\n\\u092e\\u0942\\u0932 \\u0918\\u091f\\u0915 (Block diagram \\u2014 specification, not measured):\\n\\n```\\nX \\u2208 R^{L x C}\\n   |\\n   |--[Residual extraction]---- r_0 \\u2208 R^{w x C}        (averaged over floor(L/w) whole cycles; take last w)\\n   |\\n   |--[Cycle-indexed projection, K terms]---\\n   |      for k in {0, 1, \\u2026, K-1}:   r_k \\u2208 R^{w x C}    (samples whose (t mod w) == k)\\n   |      sum(CycleIndexDecomp) restores L samples per channel\\n   |\\n   |--[Residual cycle-forecasting block, per k]\\n   |      linear / small MLP on r_k[-w:] \\u2192 o_k \\u2208 R^{H x C}    (last w samples \\u092a\\u0930 apply)\\n   |\\n   |--[Invert cycle-indexed projection]---\\n   |      for k in {0,1,\\u2026,H-1}: assign each target step h to offset index (h mod w), gathering o_{k}[h]\\n   |\\n   |--[Linear / projection head]--\\u2192 \\u0176 \\u2208 R^{H x C}\\n```\\n\\n### \\u0918\\u091f\\u0915-\\u0926\\u0930-\\u0918\\u091f\\u0915 \\u0935\\u093f\\u0928\\u093f\\u0930\\u094d\\u0926\\u0947\\u0936\\n\\n| \\u0918\\u091f\\u0915 | Specification | Default | Optional arm | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Residual extraction (single) | epoch-wise averaging of full-cycle subsequences; last w rows retained | ON | \\u2014 | Baseline depth; canonical \\\"1-cycle residual\\\" |\\n| Multi-cycle residual decomposition | \\u090a\\u092a\\u0930 \\u091c\\u0948\\u0938\\u093e, \\u092a\\u0930 K = w \\u092a\\u0942\\u0930\\u094d\\u0923 cycle indices | OFF (main run) | Arm (b) in (h) | Specification says K dim \\u092a\\u0930 ablate |\\n| Cycle-indexed projection | (t mod w) \\u0926\\u094d\\u0935\\u093e\\u0930\\u093e index, \\u091a\\u0948\\u0928\\u0932-\\u0935\\u093e\\u0930 | ON | \\u2014 | Implementation note: efficient reshape [B, L//w, w, C] indexed operation |\\n| Forecasting block (residual cycle-forecasting) | per-(index, channel) linear: R^C \\u2192 R^C, \\u092f\\u093e two-layer linear (linear-activation-linear) \\u091c\\u092c DLinear-\\u091c\\u0948\\u0938\\u093e \\u0938\\u092e\\u093e\\u0928\\u0924\\u093e \\u091a\\u093e\\u0939\\u093f\\u090f; positional encoding \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 (canonical CycleNet minimalism) | 2-layer linear | \\u2014 | depth ~ (2\\u20133) stacked linear as MLP arm |\\n| Linear / projection head | final R^{H x C} assembled by gather-on-cycle-index | ON | per-channel independent vs shared head \\u2014 Arm (f) | H \\u2264 720, \\u0938\\u092d\\u0940 horizons \\u090f\\u0915 head \\u092a\\u0930 stacked |\\n| Instance normalization (channel-wise) | per-window mean/std on inputs only, inverse-applying on output (RevIN-style per-window affine) | OFF (main run) | Arm (d) in (h) | Main-run normalization = plain train stats per channel |\\n| Multi-scale CycleNet stacking | parallel cycles at w_1, w_2, \\u2026; predictions averaged/summed | OFF (main run) | Arm (c) in (h), NICE-TO-HAVE | \\u0905\\u0917\\u0930 matrix overflow \\u0915\\u0930\\u0947 \\u0924\\u094b future-work \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 relegate; explicit assumption |\\n| Positional encoding | \\u2014 | OFF | \\u2014 | Canonical CycleNet \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 |\\n\\n### \\u0905\\u0902\\u0926\\u0930 \\u0915\\u0947 design variables \\u091c\\u093f\\u0928\\u094d\\u0939\\u0947\\u0902 report \\u0915\\u0930\\u0928\\u093e \\u0939\\u0948\\n\\n- K (residual decomposition depth) \\u2014 main value = K = w; ablation \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 1, 2, 4, w \\u0915\\u0940 grid \\u092a\\u0930\\u0964\\n- Period source \\u2208 {fixed w, FFT-autocorr-detected w} \\u2014 main = fixed; ablation arm (a)\\u0964\\n- Normalization \\u2208 {per-channel train stats, RevIN-like per-window affine} \\u2014 main = train stats; arm (d)\\u0964\\n- Head \\u2208 {shared linear, per-channel independent linear} \\u2014 arm (f)\\u0964\\n- Loss \\u2208 {MSE, MAE} \\u2014 main = MSE; arm (e)\\u0964\\n\\n### Implementation assumptions vs well-supported facts\\n\\n- Well-supported (high level): lookback \\u0915\\u094b residual + period-index terms \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 decompose \\u0915\\u0930\\u0928\\u093e, \\u0905\\u0902\\u0924\\u093f\\u092e w samples \\u092a\\u0930 forecasting block, \\u0914\\u0930 linear head \\u2014 \\u092f\\u0939 design \\u0938\\u093f\\u0926\\u094d\\u0927\\u093e\\u0902\\u0924\\u0903 canonical CycleNet description \\u0938\\u0947 \\u092e\\u0947\\u0932 \\u0916\\u093e\\u0924\\u093e \\u0939\\u0948\\u0964\\n- Assumptions (\\u090a\\u092a\\u0930 default \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0930\\u0942\\u092a \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 \\u0932\\u0949\\u0915 \\u0915\\u093f\\u090f \\u0917\\u090f): exact decomposition depth K = w, multi-block linear forecasting vs MLP, multi-scale stacking as optional only, RevIN opt-in via ablation arm only; positional encoding excluded; multi-channel joint prediction shared head as main\\u0964\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (c) Datasets and period assumptions \\u2014 table\\n\\n| Dataset | Sampling | Canonical w | Periodicity interpretation | Data access (design runtime) |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| ETTh1 | hourly | w = 24 | daily cycle (and 7\\u00d724 = 168 weekly secondary) | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\\n| ETTh2 | hourly | w = 24 | daily | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\\n| ETTm1 | 15-min | w = 96 | daily | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\\n| ETTm2 | 15-min | w = 96 | daily | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\\n| Weather | 10-min | w = 144 | daily | download infeasible (sandbox, no network) |\\n| Exchange | business-day | w = 5 | weekly, business-day | download infeasible (sandbox, no network) |\\n| Electricity | hourly | w = 24 | daily | download infeasible (sandbox, no network) |\\n| Traffic | hourly | w = 24 | daily | download infeasible (sandbox, no network) |\\n| ILI | weekly | w = 52 | yearly | design-only; data fetch execution prerequisite |\\n\\nAssumption (explicit): \\u091a\\u0942\\u0901\\u0915\\u093f bubblewrap sandbox \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 network disabled \\u0939\\u0948, \\u0907\\u0938\\u0932\\u093f\\u090f Electricity / Traffic / Weather / Exchange \\u0915\\u0947 datasets \\u0907\\u0938 design phase \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 download \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0915\\u093f\\u090f \\u091c\\u093e \\u0938\\u0915\\u0924\\u0947\\u0964 \\u0907\\u0928 datasets \\u0915\\u0940 \\u0938\\u092d\\u0940 \\u0938\\u0902\\u0916\\u094d\\u092f\\u093e\\u090f\\u0901 design-time specification \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902, measured \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902\\u0964 \\u092f\\u0939 explicit execution prerequisite \\u0928\\u094b\\u091f \\u0939\\u0948 \\u2014 \\u0915\\u094b\\u0908 measurement \\u092f\\u093e runtime test \\u0907\\u0928\\u0915\\u0947 \\u0932\\u093f\\u090f \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0915\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u0917\\u092f\\u093e\\u0964\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (d) Task formulation\\n\\n| Item | Specification |\\n|---|---|\\n| Input | X \\u2208 R^{L x C}, sliding window with stride = H (training) = H (test, val) |\\n| Target | Y \\u2208 R^{H x C} |\\n| Horizons H | ETT/Exchange/Weather/Electricity/Traffic \\u2192 {96, 192, 336, 720}; ILI \\u2192 {24, 36, 48, 60} |\\n| Lookback L | tuned over {96, 192, 336, 720} with constraint L % w == 0; selected best on validation MSE per L-grid; report L per dataset |\\n| Reporting variant | Primary: multivariate (all C channels jointly); Secondary, labelled: univariate on OT column for ETTh*/ETTm* families |\\n| Normalization (main) | per-channel mean/std from training split only; applied to inputs; targets inverse-transformed at evaluation |\\n| Normalization (RevIN ablation) | per-window mean/std on inputs, inverse on outputs; computed inside each window at train and inference |\\n| Padding of first L samples | no padding; forecast window generation starts from index L onwards \\u2014 earlier samples simply not consumed |\\n| Splits \\u2014 train/val/test | ETT h: 7:1:2; ETT m: 6:2:2; Electricity/Traffic: 70/10/20 (default; alternative 60/20/20 declared at execution); Weather/Exchange: standard benchmark splits; ILI: standard splits; strict time-disjoint, no rolling leak |\\n| Rolling-leak safeguard | test windows generated with stride = H (no overlap); validation set also stride = H |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (e) Training / optimization recipe\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Optimizer | Adam, amsgrad=False (default) |\\n| Weight decay | \\u2208 {1e-4, 1e-5} (treat as small grid; default = 1e-4) |\\n| Learning-rate schedule | cosine from peak lr \\u2208 {1e-3, 5e-4, 1e-4} to ~1% of peak over training; alternative one-cycle mentioned but default = cosine |\\n| Mini-batch size | \\u2208 {32, 64} (baseline = 32) |\\n| Epochs | budget cap \\u2208 {100, 200} (default cap = 100); early-stopping on validation MSE with patience = 10 epochs |\\n| Loss (backprop) | MSE on standardized targets |\\n| Loss (evaluation) | MSE and MAE on original scale; L1 backprop reported as ablation arm (e) |\\n| Gradient clipping | max-norm 1.0 |\\n| Seed protocol | N_seeds = 3; mean \\u00b1 std across seeds reported for every (dataset, horizon, metric) |\\n| Threading | 24 CPU threads at process start; explicit torch.set_num_threads(24) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (f) Evaluation protocol and metrics\\n\\nPrimary metrics:\\n- MSE on standardized targets (so backprop MSE = eval MSE up to scaling); used in all tables as primary.\\n- MAE on the original (un-standardized) scale; reported alongside MSE.\\n\\nProtocol:\\n- Multi-horizon rolling evaluation over all test windows with stride = H (no window overlap). For each window, predict H future steps; concatenate per-step metrics across windows to produce per-step (1\\u2026H) and aggregated per-horizon statistics.\\n- Aggregation: per-horizon MSE and MAE (matched to H = {96, 192, 336, 720}); plus unweighted mean across horizons (the scalar that enters comparison-vs-DLinear test).\\n\\nReporting granularity:\\n- Per (dataset, horizon, metric, seed) and the per-row mean \\u00b1 std across seeds (= 3).\\n- Primary table = multivariate; secondary table = univariate (OT column on ETT families only).\\n\\nReporting variant \\u2014 univariate (ablation-by-convention only):\\n- For ETTh*/ETTm*: univariate forecasts on the OT column alone, with same H, L, normalization protocol; reported in a separate, labelled table.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (g) Baselines\\n\\n| Baseline | Definition | Required | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| NAIVE-last | \\u0177[t+1:t+H] = x[t] (last observed value broadcast over H) | Yes \\u2014 must-include | Standard sanity floor |\\n| NAIVE-seasonal-w | \\u0177[t+h] = x[t+h-w] (shifted to fall inside [t-w+1, t]) | Yes \\u2014 must-include | Matches CycleNet's claim: period matters |\\n| DLinear | two parallel linear regressors on (i) moving-average trend (K_avg) and (ii) detrended series, summed; horizon produced by Linear(L \\u2192 H) per channel (joint linear when multitask) | Yes \\u2014 must-include | DLinear is the closest published reference; comparison floor for \\\"better than DLinear\\\" claims |\\n| Transformer-family reference | vanilla Transformer forecaster (input projection, positional encoding or RoPE-like, encoder-only, head = linear) | Nice-to-have \\u2014 discussion only | \\u092f\\u0926\\u093f compute budget tight \\u0939\\u0948 \\u0924\\u094b explicitly \\\"out of scope, future work\\\" declare \\u0915\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u091c\\u093e\\u092f; \\u0915\\u094b\\u0908 number fabricate \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0915\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u091c\\u093e\\u092f\\u0917\\u093e |\\n\\nOut-of-scope for this design: \\u0915\\u094b\\u0908 \\u092d\\u0940 Transformer \\u091c\\u093f\\u0938\\u0915\\u0947 \\u0932\\u093f\\u090f params tune \\u0915\\u0930\\u0928\\u093e \\u092f\\u093e \\u091c\\u091f\\u093f\\u0932 architectural choice \\u0906\\u0935\\u0936\\u094d\\u092f\\u0915 \\u0939\\u094b (FEDformer / Informer \\u0906\\u0926\\u093f) \\u2014 \\u0915\\u0947\\u0935\\u0932 discussion bullet \\u0924\\u0915 \\u0938\\u0940\\u092e\\u093f\\u0924\\u0964\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (h) Ablation matrix with priority\\n\\n| Priority | Arm | Variable | Levels | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| (a) | fixed w vs auto-detected w | period source | {fixed canonical, FFT/autocorrelation peak} | Run on ETTh1 / ETTh2 / ETTm1 / ETTm2 / ILI (5 datasets); default = fixed on the rest |\\n| (b) | residual decomposition depth K | K | {1, 2, 4, K = w} (with K = w being main) | Run on every dataset |\\n| (c) | multi-scale stacking | on/off | {off, w1=w, w2=7w (when 7w \\u2264 L)} | NICE-TO-HAVE; relegate to \\\"future-work\\\" paragraph if matrix overflows |\\n| (d) | normalization | per-channel train stats vs RevIN-like window-wise affine | {train-stats, RevIN} | Run on every dataset |\\n| (e) | loss | MSE vs MAE | {MSE, MAE} | Sensitivity check, single horizon = 96 only, to bound cost |\\n| (f) | head | shared linear vs per-channel independent linear | {shared, per-channel} | Run on every dataset |\\n\\nTotal size-bound (qualitative): main run base = 9 datasets \\u00d7 4 horizons \\u00d7 3 seeds (specifications only). Priority ablations (a)+(b)+(d)+(f) multiply this by approximately the product of per-arm grid sizes 2, 2, 2, 2 \\u2014 order-of-magnitude low-to-mid hundreds of CPU-hours (qualitative, no fabricated figures). Sensitivity arm (e) at H = 96 only adds a single-horizon extra layer.\\n\\nHard shrink protocol (explicit, if matrix overflows the budget once a CPU-hour ceiling is given):\\n1. \\u092a\\u0939\\u0932\\u0947 drop multi-scale arm (c) \\u2014 relocate to future-work paragraph (matches NICE-TO-HAVE tag).\\n2. \\u0909\\u0938\\u0915\\u0947 \\u092c\\u093e\\u0926 drop sensitivity arm (e) L1 \\u2014 relocate to future-work.\\n3. \\u0905\\u0902\\u0924\\u093f\\u092e \\u0928\\u093f\\u0930\\u094d\\u0923\\u092f \\u2014 N_seeds \\u0915\\u094b 3 \\u2192 2 \\u0918\\u091f\\u093e\\u090f\\u0901 only on low-priority arms; \\u0939\\u092e\\u0947\\u0936\\u093e 3 seeds main run \\u092a\\u0930 \\u092c\\u0928\\u0947 \\u0930\\u0939\\u0947\\u0902\\u0917\\u0947\\u0964\\n\\nFinal hard-cap enforcement (assumptions explicitly listed):\\n- Data download bubblewrap \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 infeasible; \\u0915\\u093f\\u0938\\u0940 \\u092d\\u0940 dataset \\u0915\\u093e raw CSVs \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0938\\u093e\\u0925 training execution \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0932\\u093f\\u090f spec \\u0915\\u0940 \\u0917\\u0908 \\u0939\\u0948, \\u092a\\u0930 design deliverable \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 downloaded/measured \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0939\\u0948\\u0964\\n- Total ABI post-shrink target: specification only \\u2014 no fabricated number; researcher \\u0926\\u094d\\u0935\\u093e\\u0930\\u093e CPU-hour budget \\u0926\\u093f\\u090f \\u091c\\u093e\\u0928\\u0947 \\u092a\\u0930 \\u092f\\u0947 numbers finalized \\u0939\\u094b\\u0902\\u0917\\u0947\\u0964\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (i) Controls (including leakage checks) and seed protocol\\n\\nUniversal controls applied to every compared model and every ablation:\\n\\n| Control | Description |\\n|---|---|\\n| Random seeds | fixed set S = {s1, s2, s3}; s1 is the canonical seed; reproducible init everywhere (numpy, torch CPU) |\\n| Splits | train/val/test identical indices across all compared models |\\n| L, H, w, normalization statistics | identical across all models |\\n| Pipeline (cycle-indexed projection shape, head dimension) | identical constants |\\n| Loss / eval transform | identical |\\n\\nLeakage checks (explicit):\\n\\n| Check | How |\\n|---|---|\\n| Train/val/test time-disjoint | partitions strictly by index; train before val before test (no shuffling that mixes future into past) |\\n| No future in normalization | per-channel mean/std are computed on training rows only, then applied to all splits |\\n| No rolling leak between consecutive test windows | stride = H; forecast windows do not overlap on the input side; no shared input rows between two windows |\\n| No future in cycle-indexed projection | projection operates only on lookback X; targets Y are not indexed into the projection |\\n| No data leakage between ablation arms | each arm re-initializes from the same s1 (and s2, s3); no warm-start across arms |\\n\\nSeed protocol:\\n- Per (model, dataset, horizon, metric): report mean \\u00b1 std across S.\\n- Comparisons use paired seeds (same si for the model and its control).\\n- Failed seeds (nan, inf, abrupt divergence) explicitly enumerated; if a seed fails it is replaced and the failure logged \\u2014 no silent replacement.\\n\\nNecessary diagnostics (recorded per run, not used for selection bias):\\n- Train/val loss curves across epochs.\\n- Gradient norm at each step (for sanity).\\n- Initial vs final MSE gap (to confirm the model trained at all).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (j) Analysis plan\\n\\n### Analyzed quantities\\n\\nFor each (model M, dataset D, horizon H, seed s):\\n- multivariate MSE and MAE per horizon;\\n- unweighted mean across horizons (the scalar reported in the headline table);\\n- average across the 3 seeds (\\u03bc) and std (\\u03c3).\\n\\n### Pre-registered comparison rules\\n\\nA CycleNet-... configuration is declared \\\"better than DLinear\\\" if and only if:\\n\\n1. Headline test: at horizon H, multivariate MSE averaged across seeds \\u2014 CycleNet \\u03bc < DLinear \\u03bc (numerically better, not equal).\\n2. Sign consistency: better-than-DLinear holds in all 3 seeds (no seed where CycleNet \\u03bc > DLinear \\u03bc at the same horizon).\\n3. Magnitude reporting template (qualitative rule): difference reported as \\u0394 = (\\u03bc_c \\u2212 \\u03bc_D) \\u00b1 \\u221a(\\u03c3_c^2 + \\u03c3_D^2); the \\\"meaningfully better\\\" label is not pre-fabricated \\u2014 an explicit reporting template is pre-registered and labelled on a per-case basis at execution time.\\n4. Ablation correctness gate: main run must pass the leakage checks (i) before any \\\"better than DLinear\\\" claim is logged; any leakage deviation voids the run.\\n5. Univariate signal: secondary table \\u2014 univariate OT-only MSE on ETT families \\u2014 must be consistent in direction with multivariate main table for the same seeds, or the configuration is flagged \\\"multivariate-eligible, univariate-ineligible\\\".\\n\\n### Headline table slots\\n\\n```\\nrows:     model \\u2208 {NAIVE-last, NAIVE-seasonal-w, DLinear, CycleNet-configurations}\\ncolumns:  (dataset, horizon) pairs\\ncells:    \\u03bc \\u00b1 \\u03c3 of multivariate MSE (and MAE in a parallel mirrored table)\\n```\\n\\nSecondary tables:\\n- univariate OT MSE for ETT families;\\n- normalization arm (RevIN vs train-stats) on every dataset;\\n- fixed-w vs auto-detected-w (a-priority subset);\\n- residual decomposition depth K sweep;\\n- loss sensitivity (MSE vs MAE) at H = 96.\\n\\n### Negative-result posture\\n\\nIf CycleNet does not beat DLinear on a given dataset/horizon, the design requires honest reporting with logs of train/val curves, normalization arm results, and an explicit note in the analysis why the result may have been obtained (e.g., small dataset like ILI may favor DLinear).\\n\\n### Out-of-scope analyses (future work)\\n\\n- Auto-w arm across all nine datasets (run-on-subset only by design);\\n- Multi-scale stacking (c);\\n- Transformer-family reference (g);\\n- comparison vs FEDformer / Informer (out of scope; no reference values cited as measured here).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (k) Feasibility / risks given CPU-only bubblewrap no-network runtime\\n\\nVerified environment facts (re-checked at this turn):\\n\\n| Fact | Observation |\\n|---|---|\\n| Runtime | bubblewrap, network disabled (per task contract) |\\n| Python | 3.12.3 |\\n| Preinstalled numerical libs | none (numpy import fails) |\\n| pip3 | system /usr/bin/pip3 (v24.0) present, but no project deps preinstalled |\\n| CPU threads | 24 |\\n| Memory | ~125 GiB total, ~96 GiB available |\\n| GPU | none |\\n| Workspace | /workspace contains task.json only |\\n\\nStated execution prerequisites (NOT part of the design deliverable):\\n\\n| Prereq | What | Why |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| pip install numpy torch --index-url ... (CPU build) | numerical stack | absent today |\\n| pip install pandas | CSV/HDF5 IO | absent today |\\n| Dataset access | CSVs at canonical paths or local cache; downloads infeasible under bubblewrap | runtime constraint |\\n\\nCPU-only feasibility (qualitative, no fabricated numbers):\\n- CycleNet \\u0915\\u093e core mostly matmul + integer indexing \\u0939\\u0948, \\u0907\\u0938\\u0932\\u093f\\u090f depth \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902, \\u092c\\u0932\\u094d\\u0915\\u093f L, H, batch, dataset size dominate \\u0915\\u0930\\u0924\\u0947 \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902\\u0964\\n- For the small benchmark sizes typical of the ETTh*/ETTm*/ILI dataset subset (sub-millions of rows), total main run (without ablations) is order-of-magnitude low tens of CPU-hours on 24 threads \\u2014 this is a qualitative estimate (no per-epoch number is fabricated).\\n- For the full matrix with priority arms (a)+(b)+(d)+(f), order-of-magnitude low-to-mid hundreds of CPU-hours; shrink protocol above applies if a research budget is given.\\n- For Electricity/Traffic/Weather/Exchange: dataset sizes are larger; any unconstrained run could push into the multiple-of-hundreds range; explicit assumption \\u2014 these are listed as design specifications only, unless the user provisions data locally first.\\n\\nRisk register:\\n\\n| Risk | Mitigation in design |\\n|---|---|\\n| Network disabled \\u2014 dataset download infeasible | explicit prerequisite listing; all per-dataset numbers in this design are specification, not measurement |\\n| No preinstalled numerical libs | execution prerequisite (pip install) listed; design does not assume they are available |\\n| Compute overflow on full ablation matrix | shrink protocol in (h); main run protects first |\\n| Numerical instability (inst-norm vs train-stats mismatch) | gradient-clip = 1.0; seed protocol; RevIN isolated to a single ablation arm |\\n| Cycle-index projection misalignment when L % w != 0 | constraint L % w == 0 enforced in L grid |\\n| Per-channel independent head overparameterization on small datasets (ILI) | arm (f) reported only, not in headline |\\n| Variance masking real differences | mean \\u00b1 std across 3 seeds reported; sign-consistency gate |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (l) Explicit \\\"not run\\\" statement\\n\\n\\u092f\\u0939 \\u0926\\u0938\\u094d\\u0924\\u093e\\u0935\\u0947\\u091c\\u093c \\u0915\\u0947\\u0935\\u0932 design \\u0939\\u0948\\u0964 \\u0915\\u093f\\u0938\\u0940 \\u092d\\u0940 dataset \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0932\\u093f\\u090f \\u0915\\u094b\\u0908 training execute \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0939\\u0941\\u0908 \\u0939\\u0948, \\u0915\\u094b\\u0908 MSE/MAE measured \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0915\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u0917\\u092f\\u093e \\u0939\\u0948, \\u0914\\u0930 \\u0915\\u094b\\u0908 baseline running \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0939\\u0941\\u0908 \\u0939\\u0948\\u0964 \\u0938\\u092d\\u0940 \\u0938\\u0902\\u0916\\u094d\\u092f\\u093e\\u090f\\u0901, hyperparameter ranges, L/H grids, \\u0914\\u0930 per-dataset w values \\u2014 \\u0938\\u092c specification \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902, measured \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902\\u0964 \\\"CycleNet beats DLinear\\\" \\u091c\\u0948\\u0938\\u093e \\u0915\\u094b\\u0908 claim \\u0907\\u0938 deliverable \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0915\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u0917\\u092f\\u093e \\u0939\\u0948; comparison rules purely pre-registered \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902 \\u0914\\u0930 apply \\u0915\\u093f\\u090f \\u091c\\u093e\\u092f\\u0947\\u0902\\u0917\\u0947 \\u092f\\u0926\\u093f/\\u091c\\u092c execution \\u0939\\u094b\\u0964\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Assumption ledger (research document, beyond the resolved defaults)\\n\\nCycle-indexed gather numerics float32 \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 \\u092a\\u0930\\u094d\\u092f\\u093e\\u092a\\u094d\\u0924 assume \\u0915\\u093f\\u090f \\u0917\\u090f \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902; 24 CPU threads \\u092a\\u0930 degree-of-parallelism effective \\u092e\\u093e\\u0928\\u093e \\u0917\\u092f\\u093e \\u0939\\u0948 (\\u091b\\u094b\\u091f\\u0947 linear layer batch \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 CPU contention \\u0938\\u0947 \\u092a\\u094d\\u0930\\u092d\\u093e\\u0935\\u093f\\u0924 \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902), wider grid \\u092a\\u0930 re-evaluate \\u0915\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u091c\\u093e\\u092f\\u0917\\u093e; standard benchmark splits (ETT 7:1:2 / 6:2:2, Electricity/Traffic 70/10/20) reproducing-published conditions \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0932\\u093f\\u090f \\u0915\\u093e\\u092b\\u093c\\u0940 \\u092e\\u093e\\u0928\\u0947 \\u0917\\u090f \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902, CSV version mismatch \\u092a\\u0930 anchor-by-date protocol \\u092a\\u0930 host \\u0938\\u0947 confirmation \\u0906\\u0935\\u0936\\u094d\\u092f\\u0915 \\u0939\\u0948; per-channel independent vs shared head arm (f) \\u090f\\u0915 diagnostic \\u0939\\u0948, headline \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902; FFT/autocorrelation-based period detection arm (a) \\u0915\\u0940 implementation detail \\u0915\\u094b FFT magnitude peak (\\u2265 0.5 \\u00d7 Nyquist) \\u092f\\u093e ACF lag-w peak (\\u2265 0.5 of dominant lag) \\u0924\\u0915 restricted \\u0915\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u0917\\u092f\\u093e \\u0939\\u0948, exact scipy/numpy FFT signature \\u092a\\u0930 locked \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0939\\u0948\\u0964\\n\\n### Open items (next-turn decision if user requests)\\n\\nTransformer-family reference formally listed baseline \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 \\u0939\\u0948 \\u092f\\u093e future work \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 relegate \\u092f\\u093e drop \\u2014 current default = future work, \\u092a\\u0930 lock \\u0928\\u0939\\u0940\\u0902 \\u0939\\u0941\\u0906; CPU-hour budget ceiling \\u0906\\u0928\\u0947 \\u092a\\u0930 shrink protocol trigger threshold re-evaluate \\u0915\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u091c\\u093e\\u092f\\u0917\\u093e; headline matrix \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 Electricity/Traffic \\u0915\\u0940 retention \\u0915\\u093e \\u0928\\u093f\\u0930\\u094d\\u0923\\u092f execution \\u0938\\u0947 \\u092a\\u0939\\u0932\\u0947 local cache provisioning \\u092a\\u0930 depend \\u0915\\u0930\\u0924\\u093e \\u0939\\u0948\\u0964\", \"evidence\": \"Workspace contents under /workspace: only task.json is present (\\u2248395 bytes). `track.md` is the documents.track.md field inside task.json with the single-line content 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.' Verified runtime: bubblewrap (no network); python3 --version \\u2192 Python 3.12.3; `import numpy` fails with ModuleNotFoundError; system pip3 v24.0 exists but no project deps installed; nproc \\u2192 24; free -h \\u2192 ~125 GiB RAM total, ~96 GiB available; no GPU. All numerical claims in the design are specifications only \\u2014 no execution occurred, no measure taken, no fabricated per-epoch times reported.\", \"assumptions\": [\"Data access for Electricity/Traffic/Weather/Exchange is infeasible in bubblewrap, so per-dataset numbers in this design are specification, not measurement.</item>\\n<item>Datasets ETTh*/ETTm*/ILI are listed as design-time specifications pending execution-time data access (CSV/HDF5 at canonical paths).</item>\\n<item>Cycle-indexed projection implementation assumed to be efficient via reshape [B, L//w, w, C] and gather; exact code deferred to execution.</item>\\n<item>CycleNet canonical high-level idea (residual + period-indexed decomposition, forecast on last w, linear head) is taken as well-supported; depth K, multi-scale stacking opt-in, RevIN opt-in, no positional encoding are design choices, not source-confirmed facts.</item>\\n<item>Standard benchmark splits (ETT 7:1:2 / 6:2:2, Electricity/Traffic 70/10/20) are assumed to be the canonical splits; CSV version mismatch requires anchor-by-date confirmation at execution.</item>\\n<item>CPU-only feasibility estimate is qualitative (low-tens to low-hundreds of CPU-hours) \\u2014 no fabricated per-epoch or per-run numbers.</item>\\n<item>Float32 numerics are sufficient for cycle-indexed gather; fp16/bf16 not considered because GPU is absent.</item>\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"CPU-hour budget ceil